The repo map in the system prompt now respects --deny-dir and --allow-dir. It's committed as 0c855e9d, ending with Part of #1002.

The leak: I reproduced it before changing anything, in a temp git repo with private/keys.rs and src/ok.rs:

| yoyo --deny-dir <abs>/proj/private --print-system-prompt | before | after |
|---|---|---|
| grep -c plain_private_qq4 (denied file's symbol) | 1 | 0 |
| grep -c ok_fn_qq4 (allowed sibling) | 1 | 1 |

Run with no fence, the output is the same as before and prints no warning. With the fence it prints one stderr line: ⚠ repo map omitted 1 file blocked by the directory fence (--deny-dir/--allow-dir).

What changed:
• **`src/commands_map.rs:** all repo-map builds now go through one shared function. Each file's absolute path is checked with the existing DirectoryRestrictions::check_path`, which already resolves symlinks, so I didn't write a second resolver. The check runs **before** the file is read, so a denied file's symbols are never extracted.
  • The warning gives only a count, never file names, since names would leak what the fence hides. It shows even in quiet mode, like the instruction-file and goal refusals, and uses no glyphs in plain output.
  • With no fence, the output is byte-identical to before.
• **The old unfenced prompt function** was left with no production caller, so it's now test-only. No shipped path can build the prompt map without the fence.
• **`/map`** is unchanged. It's a display for the user, not something sent to the model.
• **`src/cli.rs:** one edit, passing the existing dir_restrictions` into the call.

Tests (temp dirs only, never this repo):
• a denied plain subdirectory, with an exact-string check that the allowed sibling still appears
• a symlink pointing into a denied directory
• the same symlink under --allow-dir <proj> alone
• no fence gives identical output
• the warning text table
• each absence test first confirms the unfenced map really contains the symbol, so a pass can't come from an empty fixture

For the positive control, I disabled the check_path call, mutating and restoring in one command. Exactly the two deny tests failed, by name. After restoring, no NEUTERED marker is left.

Checks: build, clippy with -D warnings, fmt --check, and the full cargo test all pass (6013 unit tests and every other suite, 0 failed).

Docs: I added the missing commands_map.rs entry to ARCHITECTURE.md, including the residue list, and a bullet to docs/src/configuration/permissions.md.

Still not fixed (#1002 stays open):
• The file listing and recently-changed list in the prompt still show denied files' names, though not their contents. That's in context.rs.
• The memory.json fence is untouched.
• I haven't checked skills.
• `--safe-mode` still includes the repo map, which is a separate decision.
